          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#topology Topology
          %p
            The ring of
            = succeed "-adic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                As a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+disconnected+space"} totally disconnected
                (i.e., is a
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+space"} Stone space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accumulation+point"} accumulation point
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clopen+set"} clopen sets
                – a Stone space with these properties must be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cantor+space"} Cantor space
            %li
              %p
                As a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
                under addition, it is therefore an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+connected+group"} almost connected group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+group"} compact group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+duality"} Pontryagin dual
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%C3%BCfer+group"} Prüfer
                = succeed "-group" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
